---
import PageLayout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Eyebrow from '~/components/Eyebrow.astro';
import GradientOrb from '~/components/GradientOrb.astro';

const sections = [
  ['what-we-collect', 'What we collect'],
  ['why', 'Why we process it'],
  ['cctv', 'Video surveillance (CCTV)'],
  ['sharing', 'Who we share it with'],
  ['protection', 'How we protect it'],
  ['retention', 'How long we keep it'],
  ['rights', 'Your rights under RA 10173'],
  ['website', 'This website specifically'],
  ['dpo', 'How to contact the DPO'],
];
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy Notice" description="How the Iloilo Science and Technology University and Community Multi-Purpose Cooperative collects, uses, protects, and shares personal data across all its services, per RA 10173 (Data Privacy Act of 2012).">
  <section class="screen-hero relative bg-navy text-white overflow-hidden">
    <GradientOrb position="top-right" size="md" intensity={0.2} />
    <div class="container-page py-16 md:py-24 relative">
      <Eyebrow color="orange">Data privacy</Eyebrow>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl md:text-5xl text-white max-w-3xl">Privacy Notice</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-white/80 max-w-2xl">Cooperative-wide · Version 2026-08 · Effective 1 October 2026</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container-page py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-10 text-ink leading-relaxed">
      <header class="print-letterhead" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="lh-rule"></div>
        <div class="lh-body">
          <img src="/logo.svg" alt="" class="lh-seal" />
          <div class="lh-ident">
            <p class="lh-name">Iloilo Science and Technology University and<br />Community Multi-Purpose Cooperative (ISATUCMPC)</p>
            <div class="lh-meta">
              <div>Burgos St., La Paz, Iloilo City<br />Phone: 330-2586<br />Registered with CDA Iloilo Extension Office</div>
              <div>CDA Reg. No. 9520-06008210 &middot; CIN: 106060939<br />TIN: 005-440-349<br />isatucmpc1964@gmail.com &middot; www.isatucmpc.coop</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="lh-rule"></div>
        <p class="lh-eyebrow">ISATU and Community Multi-Purpose Cooperative</p>
        <h2 class="lh-title">Privacy Notice</h2>
        <p class="lh-sub">Cooperative-wide &middot; Version 2026-08 &middot; Effective 1 October 2026</p>
      </header>

      <p class="no-print text-right">
        <button type="button" id="printNotice" class="border border-navy text-navy rounded px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold bg-white cursor-pointer">
          Print this notice
        </button>
      </p>

      <div class="bg-brand-bg border-t-[3px] border-orange rounded-b-lg p-6">
        <p><strong class="font-display text-navy">Data Protection Officer (DPO):</strong> Elma E. Liza, Finance Head<br />
          Iloilo Science and Technology University<br />and Community Multi-Purpose Cooperative<br />
          Burgos St., La Paz, Iloilo City<br />
          CDA Reg. No. 9520-06008210</p>
      </div>

      <p>This Notice explains how the Iloilo Science and Technology University (ISAT U) and Community Multipurpose Cooperative (&ldquo;ISATUCMPC&rdquo;, &ldquo;the Cooperative&rdquo;, &ldquo;we&rdquo;) collects, uses, protects, and shares your personal data, and the rights you have under <strong>Republic Act No. 10173 (Data Privacy Act of 2012)</strong> and the rules of the National Privacy Commission (NPC).</p>

      <p>It applies to <strong>all our services and ventures</strong>: membership, savings and time deposits, loans, the convenience store and our other retail and food outlets, the boarding houses, the copy center, the laundry, and this website. The Member Portal (MemberFolio) shows its own notice inside the portal.</p>

      <nav aria-label="On this page" class="bg-brand-bg rounded-lg p-6">
        <p class="font-display text-navy">On this page</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2 list-none pl-0 text-sm">
          {sections.map(([id, label]) => (
            <li><a href={`#${id}`} class="text-navy underline underline-offset-2">{label}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </nav>

      <div id="what-we-collect" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl text-navy">What we collect</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
          <li><strong>Members and applicants</strong> — identity details (name, birth date, civil status, address, contact numbers), government-issued IDs, beneficiaries, share capital, savings, and loan records. Some of this is <strong>sensitive personal information</strong>; we tell you at the form when it is.</li>
          <li><strong>Borrowers and co-makers</strong> — financial capacity, employment and payroll details, and your credit history with the Cooperative, collected with your authorization each time you apply for a loan.</li>
          <li><strong>Employees and job applicants</strong> — 201-file records, government IDs, compensation, and time-and-attendance records.</li>
          <li><strong>Boarders</strong> — boarder profile and registration details, guardian contacts, and billing records.</li>
          <li><strong>Store and loyalty customers</strong> — sales transaction records; and, if you enroll in the student loyalty program, your name and student ID.</li>
          <li><strong>Visitors to our premises</strong> — video images recorded by our CCTV cameras at the main office, our stores, the canteen, the boarding house, and the laundry. See <a href="#cctv" class="text-navy underline underline-offset-2">Video surveillance</a> below.</li>
          <li><strong>Website visitors</strong> — only what you type into our forms. The detail is in <a href="#website" class="text-navy underline underline-offset-2">the section on this website</a> below.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div id="why" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl text-navy">Why we process it</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">We process personal data to: establish and manage your membership; open and service your savings, time deposits, and loans; bill and collect what is due; run our stores, boarding houses, and other ventures; pay and manage our employees; comply with the Philippine Cooperative Code and the regulations of the CDA, BIR, DOLE, and other authorities; protect the Cooperative against fraud; and, only if you separately opt in, send you SMS updates.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">We ask for consent where the law requires it, and we <strong>never bundle an optional consent with a required one</strong>. You may withdraw an optional consent at any time.</p>
      </div>

      <div id="cctv" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl text-navy">Video surveillance (CCTV)</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">We operate closed-circuit television (CCTV) cameras at five of our locations: the <strong>main office, our stores, the canteen, the boarding house, and the laundry</strong>. The cameras record video images of anyone on those premises — members, employees, boarders, customers, and visitors — for the security of persons and property and to investigate incidents such as theft, damage, or accidents. We do <strong>not</strong> use the cameras to monitor individual employee performance.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">Recordings are held on equipment kept on our own premises. They are <strong>not stored in the cloud</strong>, and <strong>no outside company monitors or views them</strong>. Footage is overwritten on a rolling <strong>20-day</strong> cycle; a recording is kept beyond that only where it has been preserved for a specific incident, and then only for as long as that incident or case requires. Access is limited to authorized staff, and we release footage outside the Cooperative only to law enforcement or a court on lawful request.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">You may ask the Data Protection Officer whether footage of you exists and to see it. Because CCTV footage almost always shows other people as well, we may need to protect their images, or limit what we can show you, before we can act on the request.</p>
      </div>

      <div id="sharing" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl text-navy">Who we share it with</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">We share personal data only with:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
          <li><strong>Regulators and authorities</strong> when the law requires — CDA, BIR, DOLE, NPC, courts, and law enforcement on lawful order</li>
          <li><strong>Our federation and program partners</strong> — such as NATCCO and insurers for member coverage — to the extent your membership or a program you joined requires</li>
          <li><strong>Service providers</strong> that operate our systems under contract and only on our instructions: our applications are hosted with a cloud provider in <strong>Singapore</strong>, our emails are delivered by a transactional email provider, and this website is delivered through a content network</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4"><strong>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal data</strong>, and we do not use it for third-party marketing.</p>
      </div>

      <div id="protection" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl text-navy">How we protect it</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">Our systems are served only over encrypted connections (HTTPS), access is per-person and limited by role, financial and membership transactions are audit-trailed, and databases are backed up on a defined cadence. Paper records are kept in locked cabinets in staff-only areas. Our full security measures are set out in the Cooperative&rsquo;s Privacy Manual, which the Board adopted alongside this Notice.</p>
      </div>

      <div id="retention" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl text-navy">How long we keep it</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">We keep records only as long as the purpose and the law require: membership and loan records for the periods set by cooperative and tax regulations after your membership or loan ends, payroll and accounting records for the periods set by the BIR and DOLE, CCTV footage for 20 days on a rolling cycle, and website form submissions briefly unless they become part of a membership record. When a retention period lapses, records are securely shredded or deleted.</p>
      </div>

      <div id="rights" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl text-navy">Your rights under RA 10173</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">You have the right to:</p>
        <ol class="mt-4 list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3">
          <li><strong>Be informed</strong> about how your personal data is processed (this notice)</li>
          <li><strong>Access</strong> the data we hold about you — request a copy from the DPO</li>
          <li><strong>Correct</strong> inaccurate or outdated information</li>
          <li><strong>Erasure or blocking</strong> of unlawfully processed data, under the conditions set by law</li>
          <li><strong>Damages</strong> from unauthorized processing</li>
          <li><strong>Data portability</strong> — receive your data in a commonly used electronic format</li>
          <li><strong>Object</strong> to processing, including withdrawing an optional consent</li>
          <li><strong>File a complaint</strong> with the National Privacy Commission</li>
        </ol>
        <p class="mt-4">To exercise any of these rights, contact our Data Protection Officer. We act on verified requests within <strong>15 working days</strong>.</p>
      </div>

      <div id="website" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl text-navy">This website specifically</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">You can browse every page of <code>isatucmpc.coop</code> without giving us any personal information. We collect personal information here only when you submit one of two forms:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
          <li><strong>Membership application form</strong>: full name, date of birth, sex, <strong>civil status</strong>, contact number, email address, employment category, membership type, associate qualification, and (for associate members) the name of your recommending member. Civil status is <strong>sensitive personal information</strong> under §3(l) of RA 10173.</li>
          <li><strong>Contact form</strong>: your name, email address, and message.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">Both forms use Cloudflare Turnstile to block automated abuse; Turnstile processes technical browser signals and is covered by Cloudflare&rsquo;s privacy policy.</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
          <li>Your submission is delivered <strong>as an email to the Cooperative&rsquo;s office inbox</strong>, transmitted over encrypted connections through our email provider (Resend). You receive an acknowledgement copy at the email address you gave.</li>
          <li>The pre-filled application form (PDF) is generated <strong>inside your own browser</strong> and downloaded directly to your device — it is never uploaded to us.</li>
          <li>This website itself keeps <strong>no database of submissions</strong>, and sets <strong>no cookies at all</strong> — none for advertising, analytics, or tracking. It stores nothing in your browser.</li>
          <li>We measure how the site performs using <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>. It counts visits and records page load-speed timings so we can tell whether pages are working properly. It does <strong>not</strong> use cookies or browser storage, does <strong>not</strong> fingerprint you, and does <strong>not</strong> follow you to other websites. Your IP address reaches Cloudflare the way it reaches any website you visit; Cloudflare discards it at its nearest data center rather than storing it. What we see is aggregate counts and timings, never you as an individual.</li>
          <li>The map on our Contact page loads tiles from OpenStreetMap; your IP address is visible to OpenStreetMap when the map loads, as with any embedded map.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">We keep <strong>membership application emails</strong> until your application is decided, then as part of your membership record if you join, or disposed of if you do not proceed; and <strong>enquiry emails</strong> as long as needed to respond and follow up, then disposed of in periodic clean-ups.</p>
      </div>

      <div id="dpo" class="scroll-mt-24">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl text-navy">How to contact the DPO</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">For any privacy-related question, request, or complaint:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-6 space-y-3">
          <li><strong>Name:</strong> Elma E. Liza, Finance Head (designated DPO)</li>
          <li><strong>Office:</strong> ISATUCMPC, Burgos St., La Paz, Iloilo City</li>
          <li><strong>Phone:</strong> +63 950 108 8310</li>
          <li><strong>Email:</strong> isatucmpc1964@gmail.com</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">We commit to acknowledge your inquiry within <strong>5 working days</strong> and provide a substantive response within <strong>15 working days</strong>.</p>
        <p class="mt-4">If you are not satisfied with our response, you may file a complaint with:</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 list-disc pl-6">
          <li><strong>National Privacy Commission (NPC)</strong> — <a href="https://www.privacy.gov.ph" class="text-navy underline underline-offset-2">https://www.privacy.gov.ph</a> — complaints@privacy.gov.ph</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="text-sm text-slate"><em>Version 2026-08, adopted by Board Resolution No. 2026-08-48 and effective 1 October 2026. Changes to our privacy practices are made through a new version of this Notice, approved by the Data Protection Officer and posted on our website and at our offices. A printed copy is available from any staff member.</em></p>

      <p class="print-foot" aria-hidden="true">ISATUCMPC &middot; Cooperative-wide Privacy Notice v2026-08 &middot; printed from isatucmpc.coop/privacy</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style is:global>
    .print-letterhead, .print-foot { display: none; }

    @media print {
      @page { size: A4; margin: 15mm 18mm; }

      /* site chrome is not part of the notice */
      header:not(.print-letterhead), footer, .screen-hero, .no-print,
      nav[aria-label="On this page"] { display: none !important; }

      html, body { background: #fff !important; }
      body { font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.45; color: #111827; }
      section { padding: 0 !important; }
      .container-page { max-width: none !important; padding: 0 !important; }
      .max-w-3xl { max-width: none !important; }
      /* Tailwind v4 spaces with margin-block-end on :not(:last-child), not margin-top. */
      .space-y-10 > :not(:last-child) { margin-block-end: 11px !important; }

      .print-letterhead { display: block; margin-bottom: 10px; }
      .lh-rule { height: 2.5px; background: linear-gradient(to right, #010066, #FE9900, #FFC001); }
      .lh-body { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; padding: 10px 0 8px; }
      .lh-seal { width: 58px; height: 58px; flex: none; }
      .lh-ident { flex: 1; }
      .lh-name { margin: 0; font-family: Montserrat, sans-serif; font-size: 11.5pt; font-weight: 800;
                 line-height: 1.22; color: #010066; text-transform: uppercase; }
      .lh-meta { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 20px; margin-top: 5px;
                 font-size: 7.6pt; line-height: 1.45; color: #6B7280; }
      .lh-eyebrow { margin: 12px 0 2px; font-size: 7.6pt; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .12em;
                    text-transform: uppercase; color: #FE9900; }
      .lh-title { margin: 0; font-family: Montserrat, sans-serif; font-size: 17pt; font-weight: 800; color: #010066; }
      .lh-sub { margin: 2px 0 0; font-size: 8.6pt; color: #6B7280; }

      h2 { font-size: 11.5pt !important; margin: 10px 0 4px !important; color: #010066 !important;
           border-bottom: 1.2px solid #E8E8E8; padding-bottom: 2px; break-after: avoid; }
      h2 + p, h2 + ul, h2 + ol { break-before: avoid; }
      p, li { orphans: 3; widows: 3; }
      p { margin-top: 5px !important; }
      ul, ol { margin-top: 5px !important; }
      li { margin-bottom: 2px !important; }
      a { color: #111827 !important; text-decoration: none !important; }

      /* the DPO block keeps its emphasis in print, without a heavy fill */
      .bg-brand-bg { background: #fff !important; border: 1px solid #E8E8E8;
                     border-top: 2.5px solid #FE9900 !important; padding: 8px 11px !important;
                     border-radius: 0 !important; break-inside: avoid; }

      .print-foot { display: block; margin-top: 12px; padding-top: 6px;
                    border-top: 1.2px solid #E8E8E8; font-size: 7.6pt; color: #6B7280; }
    }
  </style>

  <script>
    document.getElementById('printNotice')?.addEventListener('click', () => window.print());
  </script>
</PageLayout>
